// Arguments are evaluated in the order WRITTEN (tests/arg_order.kama), so a `give` written before a `copy`
// of the same binding has already moved it: the copy reads a moved value. Here the parameters are declared
// `a, b` and the arguments written `b, a` — the move check once walked the declared order, accepted this, and
// handed `a` an empty string.
fn string both(string a, string b) { return "${a}|${b}"; }
fn uint8 main() {
    string s = "hello";
    string r = both(b: give s, a: copy s);   // ERROR: `s` is read after the give written before it
    return cast<uint8>(r.length());
}
